## Access → Client → Website (Looker-parity mental model)

Client grants **agency Gmail** access to GA4 / GSC / Ads. Webastral does **not** import “access files”; it OAuth-connects that Gmail, syncs inventory, then maps assets:

| Looker Studio | Webastral |
|---------------|-----------|
| Log in with agency Gmail | **Connect Google** (data identity) on `/integrations` |
| GA4 Account → Property | **Client** ← Analytics account; **Website** ← each GA4 property |
| GSC Site | Same **Website** (matched by hostname / companion import) |
| Google Ads Account | **Link to existing Website** (never auto-creates client) |
| One report page per site | Top-bar **Client + Website**; charts read that website’s snapshots |
| Multi-site = pages or dropdown | Multi-property GA4 account = **one Client, many Websites**; switcher = dropdown |

Rules locked in:

1. Access = invite agency Gmail → Connect Google → Sync inventory → Import/Link
2. **1 website** → 1 Client + 1 Website; wire GA4 + GSC (+ Ads link)
3. **2+ websites same Analytics account** → 1 Client, N Websites (never 1 client per property)
4. Ads always **link to website** after Client/Website exist
5. Dashboard data is **website-scoped** snapshots (not live Looker blend); Overview can roll up Client
6. Do not mix two unrelated sites into one chart series

